    "KVCash is an internal cache that stores the relationships between pairs of tokens that a language model has already computed.",
    "When the model processes a new prompt, it repeatedly needs to recompute the same token‑to‑token relationships.",
    "By keeping those relationships in KVCash, the model can look them up instead of recalculating them, which saves compute cycles.",
    "For every pair of tokens that the model has seen, KVCash holds the pre‑computed relationship vector.",
    "On subsequent passes, the model retrieves the stored vector from KVCash rather than running the full attention calculation again.",
    "This avoids the expensive matrix multiplications that would otherwise be performed for each token pair, cutting down the number of floating‑point operations dramatically.",
    "The compression step (Headroom) reduces the number of tokens that actually reach the LLM.",
    "SRE incident debugging achieves 92 % token savings.",
    "GitHub issue try‑age achieves 73 % token savings.",
    "Code waste explanation achieves 47 % token savings.",
    "These percentages represent the reduction in tokens (and thus cost) after Headroom’s compression and the use of KVCash to avoid redundant computations."
] 

