Statements:
[
    "Headroom sits between the user and the LLM and uses the transformer’s internal attention mechanism to build a KV cache.",
    "When a sentence is fed to the model, the transformer first computes the pairwise relationships (attention scores) between every token in the context.",
    "These relationships are stored as key‑value pairs in the KV cache.",
    "For subsequent tokens, Headroom re‑uses the cached key‑value pairs that already capture the relationships between tokens that have appeared before.",
    "This reuse is what the text refers to as KVCash.",
    "Headroom then compresses the cached key‑value pairs by keeping only the most relevant relationships that actually influence the next token prediction.",
    "The compressed set of tokens is sent to the LLM, reducing the amount of data the model must process and thus cutting inference cost."
] 

